     CDS             complement(7988..10114)
                     /note="pLannotate"
                     /label="MOBA2_ECOLX"
                     /database="swissprot"
                     /identity="99.9"
                     /match_length="100.0"
                     /fragment="False"
                     /other="CDS"
                     /description="Protein evidence at protein level: Swiss-Prot
                     protein existence level 1. Part of the relaxosome complex
                     that is responsible for plasmid transfer during
                     conjugation. Locally unwinds DNA and catalyzes the cleavage
                     of one of the DNA strands at oriT. The cleaved strand is
                     then transferred through the dedicated type IV secretion
                     apparatus. MobA remains covalently linked at the 5' end of
                     the strand, and once in the recipient cell, it probably
                     catalyzes the rejoining of the two ends of the strand,
                     re-forming the circular plasmid DNA. The primase activity
                     of MobA is essential for the synthesis of primers that will
                     initiate the DNA replication events necessary to form the
                     double-stranded plasmid in the recipient cell. From
                     Escherichia coli."
